  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">STRENGTHENING THE RECOVERY OF TIGERS ACROSS THE TRANSBOUNDARY MANAS CONSERVATION AREA (TRAMCA) IN INDIA AND BHUTAN</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to (1) Reduce threats to wildlife from poaching and retaliatory killings by strengthening community engagement; (2) Facilitate policy advocacy between India and Bhutan to establish the transboundary Peace Park; and (3) Strengthen management effectiveness in TraMCA by identifying gaps using Conservation Assured Tiger Standards.</narrative>
  </description>
